0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z02-S02","name":"Zone II · Scene 2: City at Peace — The Sacred Circle & Blood-Price Trial","zone":"Z02","lines":"18.497–508","greek":"λαοὶ δ᾽ εἰν ἀγορῇ ἔσαν ἀθρόοι· ἔνθα δὲ νεῖκος ὠρώρει, δύο δ᾽ ἄνδρες ἐνείκεον εἵνεκα ποινῆς ἀνδρὸς ἀποφθιμένου... οἱ δὲ γέροντες εἵατ᾽ ἐπὶ ξεστοῖσι λίθοισ᾽ ἱερῷ ἐνὶ κύκλῳ, σκῆπτρα δὲ κηρύκων ἐν χέρσ᾽ ἔχον ἠεροφώνων· τοῖσιν ἔπειτ᾽ ἤϊσσον, ἀμοιβηδὶς δὲ δίκαζον. κεῖτο δ᾽ ἄρ᾽ ἐν μέσσοισι δύω χρυσοῖο τάλαντα, τῷ δόμεν ὃς μετὰ τοῖσι δίκην ἰθύντατα εἴποι.","buckley":"But the people were assembled in the forum, for there a strife had arisen, and two men strove for the ransom-money of a slain man; the one affirmed that he had paid all, appealing to the people, but the other denied that he had received any thing; and both wished to find a termination before a judge. The people shouted to both, supporters on either side; and the heralds reined in the people; but the elders sat upon polished stones in a sacred circle, and held in their hands the staves of the loud-shouting heralds; with these then they arose, and adjudged in turn. But there lay in the midst two talents of gold, to give to him who should pronounce a judgment the most correctly.","worldModel":{"vision":"Eight polished white stone seats arranged in a sacred circle around a kyanos pavement; two gleaming talents of gold on the central altar.","memory":"Procedural legal algorithm: blood-vendetta is converted into deliberative speech; elders rise in turn (ἀμοιβηδὶς) holding the herald’s sceptre; the two talents reward the straightest judgment (δίκην ἰθύντατα).","controller":"The polis replaces private vengeance with public arbitration."}}

